<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Disinfecting with Bleach Guide</title>
    <style>
        @page { size: A4; margin: 0; }
        .page {
            width: 794px; height: 1123px;
            padding: 50px 60px; box-sizing: border-box;
            overflow: hidden; page-break-after: always;
            position: relative;
            font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial, sans-serif;
        }
        .page:last-child { page-break-after: auto; }
        h1, h2, h3 { font-weight: bold; }
        .header-title { font-size: 36pt; line-height: 1.1; }
        .section-title { font-size: 24pt; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 20px; }
        .list-item { margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.5; }
        .footer-text { font-size: 10pt; text-align: right; }
    </style>

<style>
  @page { size: A4; margin: 0; }
  .page {
    width: 794px; height: 1123px;
    padding: 50px 60px; box-sizing: border-box;
    overflow: hidden; page-break-after: always;
    position: relative;
    font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial, "DejaVu Sans", "Liberation Sans";
  }
  .page:last-child { page-break-after: auto; }
  h1 { font-size: 24pt; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 20px; }
  h2 { font-size: 20pt; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 30px; margin-bottom: 15px; }
  p, li { font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 10px; }
  ul { padding-left: 20px; }
  .content-block { margin-bottom: 20px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="page">
        <div style="margin-bottom: 10px;">
            <span style="font-weight: bold;">Environmental Health and Safety</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="header-title">Disinfecting with bleach</h1>
        <div style="margin-top: 60px; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-end;">
            <div>
                <span style="font-size: 40pt;">ASU</span>
                <div style="font-size: 18pt; font-weight: bold;">Arizona State University</div>
            </div>
            <div class="footer-text">
                Revised {{ revision_date }}
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="page">
        <h2 class="section-title">Benefits of bleach</h2>
        <p>Bleach is also known as sodium hypochlorite:</p>
        <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
            <li class="list-item"><span data-field="benefits.benefit_1">{{ benefits.benefit_1 }}</span></li>
            <li class="list-item"><span data-field="benefits.benefit_2">{{ benefits.benefit_2 }}</span></li>
            <li class="list-item"><span data-field="benefits.benefit_3">The most common disinfectant used at {{ institution_name }}.</span></li>
            <li class="list-item"><span data-field="benefits.benefit_4">{{ benefits.benefit_4 }}</span></li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="page">
        <h2 class="section-title">Stability</h2>
        <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
            <li class="list-item"><span data-field="stability.stability_1">Diluted bleach solutions, such as {{ concentration_1 }} percent bleach in water, rapidly breakdown and quickly lose effectiveness.</span></li>
            <li class="list-item"><span data-field="stability.stability_2">Most household bleaches contain {{ concentration_2 }} percent sodium hypochlorite.</span></li>
            <li class="list-item"><span data-field="stability.stability_3">Shelf life is {{ shelf_life }} when stored at room temperature.</span></li>
            <li class="list-item"><span data-field="stability.stability_4">{{ stability.stability_4 }}</span></li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="page">
        <h2 class="section-title">Effectiveness</h2>
        <p>Always check the sodium hypochlorite concentration on the label:</p>
        <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
            <li class="list-item"><span data-field="effectiveness.concentration_range">Household bleach contains {{ concentration_range }} percent sodium hypochlorite, or {{ ppm_range }} ppm available chlorine.</span></li>
            <li class="list-item"><span data-field="effectiveness.dilution_yield">A {{ stock_concentration }} percent stock when diluted to {{ dilution_volume }} percent in water will yield a {{ yield_ppm }} ppm or a {{ yield_percent }}% hypochlorite solution.</span></li>
        </ul>
        <p>Verify if bleach is effective for the material to be disinfected because different organisms have different requirements:</p>
        <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
            <li class="list-item"><span data-field="effectiveness.kill_bacillus">100 ppm of chlorine will kill {{ bacillus_percentage }}% of {{ bacillus_organism }} spores within five minutes.</span></li>
            <li class="list-item"><span data-field="effectiveness.kill_staph">100 ppm of free chlorine inactivates {{ staph_organism }} in less than {{ staph_time }} minutes.</span></li>
            <li class="list-item"><span data-field="effectiveness.kill_myco">Higher concentrations of {{ myco_ppm }} ppm or more of chlorine are required to kill {{ myco_organism }}.</span></li>
            <li class="list-item"><span data-field="effectiveness.kill_mycoplasma">Low concentrations of {{ mycoplasma_ppm }} to {{ mycoplasma_upper_ppm }} ppm of chlorine are effective against {{ mycoplasma_organism }} and vegetative bacteria.</span></li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="page">
        <h2 class="section-title">Preparation</h2>
        <p>Always prepare bleach solutions fresh before use.</p>
        <p>For a {{ dilution_ratio }} dilution, or {{ dilution_percent }} percent solution, mix one part bleach in {{ water_parts }} parts water:</p>
        <ol style="padding-left: 20px;">
            <li class="list-item">Work in a well-ventilated area.</li>
            <li class="list-item">Wear PPE consisting of a lab coat, eye protection and gloves.</li>
            <li class="list-item">Use cold water to prevent chemical decomposition.</li>
            <li class="list-item">Label and date solution with preparation date and initials and discard after use.</li>
            <li class="list-item">Remove PPE including gloves and wash hands thoroughly.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="page">
        <h2 class="section-title">Safety</h2>
        <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
            <li class="list-item"><span data-field="safety.classification">{{ safety.classification }}</span></li>
            <li class="list-item"><span data-field="safety.mixing_warning">Chlorine solutions should never be mixed or stored with cleaning products containing {{ chemical_1 }}, {{ chemical_2 }} or {{ chemical_3 }}.</span></li>
            <li class="list-item">Know where the nearest eyewash station and emergency shower are located when working with bleach.</li>
            <li class="list-item">Review the Safety Data Sheet.</li>
            <li class="list-item"><span data-field="safety.sunlight_warning">{{ safety.sunlight_warning }}</span></li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="page">
        <h2 class="section-title">Incident response</h2>
        <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
            <li class="list-item">Avoid touching the eyes and skin when working with bleach.</li>
            <li class="list-item"><span data-field="incident.contact_eyes">{{ incident.contact_eyes }}</span></li>
            <li class="list-item"><span data-field="incident.eye_flush">If bleach gets into the eyes, immediately rinse with water for at least {{ eye_flush_time }}.</span></li>
            <li class="list-item"><span data-field="incident.skin_flush">If skin comes in contact with bleach, rinse with lukewarm water for at least {{ skin_flush_time }}.</span></li>
            <li class="list-item"><span data-field="incident.inhalation">{{ incident.inhalation }}</span></li>
            <li class="list-item"><span data-field="incident.ingestion_inhalation">{{ incident.ingestion_inhalation }}</span></li>
            <li class="list-item"><span data-field="incident.exposure_protocol">{{ incident.exposure_protocol }}</span></li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="page">
        <h2 class="section-title" style="text-align: center;">Important considerations</h2>
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-around; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 40px;">
            <div style="width: 40%;">
                <h3 style="font-size: 24pt; margin-bottom: 30px;">Bleach</h3>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li class="list-item"><span data-field="considerations.inactivation">{{ considerations.inactivation }}</span></li>
                    <li class="list-item"><span data-field="considerations.discoloration">{{ considerations.discoloration }}</span></li>
                    <li class="list-item"><span data-field="considerations.corrosion">Is corrosive to metals at concentrations greater than {{ corrosion_ppm }}.</span></li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div style="width: 50%; text-align: center; font-size: 100pt; color: #FFC72C;">
                &#123;
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

<style>
  @page { size: A4; margin: 0; }
  .page {
    width: 794px; height: 1123px;
    padding: 50px 60px; box-sizing: border-box;
    overflow: hidden; page-break-after: always;
    position: relative;
    font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial, "DejaVu Sans", "Liberation Sans";
  }
  .page:last-child { page-break-after: auto; }
  h1 { font-size: 24pt; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 20px; }
  h2 { font-size: 20pt; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 30px; margin-bottom: 15px; }
  p, li { font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 10px; }
  ul { padding-left: 20px; }
  .content-block { margin-bottom: 20px; }
</style>

<div class="page">
  <h1>Bleaching metal surfaces</h1>
  <div class="content-block">
    <ul>
      <li>Recalling that a standard diluted working solution is about <span data-field="concentration">{{ concentration }}</span> in the lab, if used on laboratory equipment with metal surfaces such as biological safety cabinets, be sure to wipe with <span data-field="disinfectant_concentration">{{ disinfectant_concentration }}</span> to remove residue after application.</li>
      <li>See ASU's Biosafety Cabinet Decontamination Guidelines: <a href="http://asu.edu/ehs/documents/asu-bsc-decontamination.pdf"><span data-field="guideline_link">{{ guideline_link }}</span></a>.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h1>Hazardous waste collection</h1>
  <div class="content-block">
    <p>Collect liquid waste in a clean, compatible container:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Label the container "<span data-field="waste_label">{{ waste_label }}</span>."</li>
      <li>Remove funnels and close the container when not in use.</li>
      <li>Attach a completed hazardous waste tag.</li>
      <li>Store in secondary containment in the same room where generated.</li>
      <li>When two-thirds full, request a hazardous waste pickup at <a href="http://links.asu.edu/wastepickup"><span data-field="pickup_link">{{ pickup_link }}</span></a>.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h1>Hazardous waste disposal</h1>
  <div class="content-block">
    <ul>
      <li>Chemicals that are corrosive, ignitable, reactive or toxic pose substantial or potential threats to public health or the environment.</li>
      <li>Consider all chemical waste to be a hazardous waste and do not pour down the drain or put in the trash.</li>
      <li>Approval must be received from EHS prior to drain disposal.</li>
      <li>Never autoclave bleach.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>For waste disposal information visit: <a href="http://cfo.asu.edu/waste-mgmt-and-shipping"><span data-field="disposal_info_link">{{ disposal_info_link }}</span></a>.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h1>References</h1>
  <div class="content-block">
    <ul>
      <li>ASU Biological Safety Manual: <a href="http://asu.edu/ehs/documents/biosafetymanual.pdf"><span data-field="ref_asu_manual">{{ ref_asu_manual }}</span></a></li>
      <li>World Health Organization Laboratory Biosafety Manual: <a href="http://who.int/csr/resources/publications/biosafety/Biosafety7.pdf"><span data-field="ref_who_manual">{{ ref_who_manual }}</span></a></li>
      <li>Selected EPA-Registered Disinfectants: <a href="http://epa.gov/pesticide-registration/selected-epa-registered-disinfectants"><span data-field="ref_epa_disinfectants">{{ ref_epa_disinfectants }}</span></a></li>
      <li>Protecting Workers Who Use Cleaning Chemicals: <a href="http://osha.gov/Publications/OSHA3512.pdf"><span data-field="ref_osha_guide">{{ ref_osha_guide }}</span></a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div style="text-align: center; padding-top: 50%;">
    <h1 style="font-size: 48pt; margin-bottom: 10px;">Questions?</h1>
    <p style="font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 0;">{{ contact_email }}</p>
    <p style="font-size: 14pt;">EHS: {{ phone_number }}</p>
  </div>
</div></body>
</html>